# Normalise line endings on commit.
#
# Without this file the repository stores whatever the working copy happened to have, and a tree
# edited on Windows or through a WSL mount drifts to CRLF. That drift is invisible until it reaches
# a diff: eight files in v0.5.8.3 showed as modified with 2,608 changed lines and not one real
# change among them, which makes review impossible and buries genuine edits.
#
# `text=auto` lets git decide what is text; `eol=lf` fixes what is written into a commit. Working
# copies may keep whatever endings the editor prefers - only the committed form is normalised.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Files that must never be line-ending converted, because doing so corrupts them.
*.zip  binary
*.png  binary
*.ico  binary
*.mmdb binary

# Generated or vendored files, excluded from language statistics and diff noise.
composer.lock  -diff linguist-generated
SHA256SUMS.txt -diff linguist-generated
